          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l03",
          "reminder": "The normal is perpendicular to the tangent at the same contact point."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Use the intercept and gradient conditions",
      "body": "Your normal passes through the contact point and has the stated y-intercept. Match these conditions to obtain an equation in the contact input.",
      "recap": "A line equation links its gradient, intercept and every point on the line.",
      "pitfall": "Apply the positive-gradient condition to your candidates only after deriving them.",
      "pause": "Find the candidate contact inputs, test the slope condition and simplify the permitted value.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l03",
          "reminder": "A line equation links its gradient, intercept and every point on the line."
        }
      ]
