  "solution": "<p>The derivative at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow></math>, so the normal gradient is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>. Through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> its equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p>The intercept 5 gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. The positive gradient requires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer C.</strong></p>",
